==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪsəˈpɔɪntmənt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-disappointment.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The emotion felt when a strongly held [[expectation]] is not met.
#: ''Choking back his disappointment after his own team's splendid wins against Liverpool and Aston Villa, he said: "I've got to be humble and say we were beaten by a very good side."'' &mdash; ''Today'', News Group Newspapers Ltd, 1992
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A circumstance in which a strongly held expectation is not met.
#* {{quote-news
|year=2012
|date=May 5
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Chelsea 2-1 Liverpool
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/17878435
|page=
|passage=For Liverpool, their season will now be regarded as a relative '''disappointment''' after failure to add the FA Cup to the Carling Cup and not mounting a challenge to reach the Champions League places.}}
#: ''As the disappointments crowded in &mdash; the economy, Rhodesia, strife within the trade-union movement &mdash; [[w:Harold Wilson|Wilson]] tried the expedient of a semi-formal inner Cabinet, or Parliamentary Committee, as he misleadingly liked to call it.'' &mdash; ''Cabinet'', Hennessy, Peter, Basil Blackwell Ltd, 1990

